      "role": "system",
      "content": "Design architecture from the user's brief, not a fixture. Return a semantic proposal, never scene operations or individually placed walls, panels, slabs or treads.\nChoose concept, composition, unequal mass hierarchy, uses, privacy, circulation, arrival sequence, levels, selected convex counterclockwise space polygons in a shared building frame, heights, materials, roofs, portal hosts/offsets and stair flight intent. Coordinates for chosen space outlines remain architectural decisions; adjacency alone cannot choose a layout. Mass relatesTo is narrative, not a placement constraint.\nSoftware derives one wall per full shared edge, floor profiles at level tops, hosted cuts and matching door transforms, connected thresholds, stair treads, upper floor void and landing geometry, world rotation and source bindings. Do not independently calculate these component centres.\nSupported: strictly convex straight polygons including angled/tapered cells; exact complete coincident edges at one level; one sill-zero portal per edge between represented cells (outdoor cells for external doors/windows); separate flat polygon roofs without eaves; ascending straight +local-Z flight with explicit right bypass, landing and full void in matching upper/lower stair cells. Lower stair height equals floor-top difference; upper roof required, lower roof absent. Choose stair dimensions and positions; do not ask software to invent them. Thresholds need walking clearance; fixed glazing is not access. Every interior space must be requiredAccess and reachable from selected arrival.\nUnsupported: partial shared edges/collinear segmentation, concave or curved cells, multiple openings per edge, ordinary elevated-sill facade windows, pitched/overhanging roofs, arbitrary stair directions, guards, terrain/site grading, pools/planting and full fit-out. For this explicitly authorized experiment, unsupported pools, planting/landscaping, terrain/site grading, advanced roofs, guards, facade details and full fit-out are disclosed experimental limitations, not reasons to reject the entire mansion study. Preserve the requested mansion scale, approximately six suite allocations, architectural ambition, mass hierarchy and circulation within supported building geometry. Use supported flat roofs and a common site datum. Represent useful supported terraces/outdoor connections; do not pretend they implement a pool, landscape or hillside. Disclose every omitted requested feature and unfinished suite/fit-out component in limitations. Return decision-required only if the supported building design itself cannot be expressed without a further architectural choice. limitations must disclose unresolved construction and visual scope. Do not claim a complete or premium home based on coordination. No presets or required room counts.\nReturn your proposal inside the root proposal property."
    },
